   "item": "24",
   "section": "Council Consent Items",
   "heading": "Referral: Oxford for All (Reviewed by the Facilities, Infrastructure, Transportation, Environment & Sustainability Committee)",
   "lines": [
    453,
    500
   ],
   "from": "Councilmember Tregub (Author), Councilmember Lunaparra (Co- Sponsor)",
   "contact": "Igor Tregub, Councilmember, District 4, (510) 981-7140",
   "financial_implications": "See report",
   "action": "Action: Approved revised recommendation from Councilmember Tregub in to add Councilmember Humbert as a co-sponsor and revise the recommendation to read as below. 1. Provide direction to City Manager and staff to implement city-adopted 2017 Bike Plan, the 2021 UC Berkeley Oxford St./Fulton St. Multimodal Mobility and Urban Design Study and the 2025 Bike Plan Update recommendations on Oxford Street and Fulton Street from Bancroft Way to Hearst Avenue alongside upcoming repaving. 2. Beforehand and until such permanent capital improvements are feasible, refer to the City Manager to design and construct a an interim “quick build” project if deemed feasible, prudent, and non-disruptive to permanent improvements. Improvements implemented should, at minimum, include Class IV protected bike lanes and pedestrian safety facilities. Pedestrian facilities may include daylighting, high-visibility crosswalks, curb extensions, and other improvements that increase safety for pedestrians on the corridor, informed by the above-mentioned plans. 3. Refer to the City Manager to seek funding in the amount of $400,000 from all available sources including, but not limited to the Street and Open Space Improvement Fund (SOSIP), Measure FF (2024), Long Range Development Plan (LRDP) and refer to the June budget process (FY26 Mid-Biennial Update) to provide the City of Berkeley Public Works Department with funds to support design, engineering, and construction costs for the quick build and permanent components of the project. 4. Refer to the City Manager and to The City/UC/Student Relations “4x6” Committee to explore opportunities to leverage existing and establish new financial partnerships with UC Berkeley on safety projects along Oxford Street and adjacent areas, including the Oxford and Bancroft volleyball courts project and similar initiatives.",
   "speakers": null,
   "attribution": [
    {
     "member": "off-tregub",
     "as_printed": "Councilmember Tregub (Author)",
     "role": "author",
     "order": 1
    },
    {
     "member": "off-lunaparra",
     "as_printed": "Councilmember Lunaparra (Co- Sponsor)",
     "role": "co-sponsor",
     "order": 2
    }
   ],
   "added_cosponsors": [
    {
     "member": "off-humbert",
     "as_printed": "add Councilmember Humbert as a co-sponsor"
    }
   ],
   "motions": [],
   "prior_first_reading_vote": null
  },
